# S8 — named nd@1 binder/premise worked example (lara-syntax@0.9)
#
# This is S1's strict step with a deliberately inert beta-redex around its
# single premise citation. The named payload is:
#
#   (app (lam h (atom 1:A5:holds1:L1:228:1:C16:safety_invariant1:L1:012:1:C1:D1:L1:0) (prem e1)) (prem e1))
#
# The opaque atom key was produced with this self-contained checked command;
# zsh's @=(...)@ materializes the complete temporary Haskell source for
# @runghc@, so no untracked helper remains:
#
#   cabal exec -- runghc --ghc-arg=-isrc =(printf '%s\n' \
#     'import Lara.Prop (FunSym (..), Pred (..), Prop (..), Term (..))' \
#     'import Lara.Strict.ND (encodeAtomKey)' \
#     'main :: IO ()' \
#     'main = putStrLn (encodeAtomKey (Prop (Pred "holds") [TCon (FunSym "safety_invariant") [], TCon (FunSym "D") []]))')
#
# The frozen @nd\@1@ formula grammar requires the atom wrapper shown above.
# Section 2.2's bare-key placeholder was corrected here rather than changing
# that kernel grammar. The detour exists only to exercise binder-depth shifting; it adds no
# source-level logical strength. The two `prem e1` occurrences name the same
# source premise, but the inner one at depth 1 lowers to `(hyp 1)` and the
# outer one at depth 0 lowers to `(hyp 0)`. The opaque formula key remains the
# certificate surface's hand-hostile spot; issue #144 tracks source-level
# formula annotation authoring.
#
# The committed goldens were generated from, and byte-compared with, the
# numeric twin `(app (lam (atom 1:A5:holds1:L1:228:1:C16:safety_invariant1:L1:012:1:C1:D1:L1:0) (hyp 1)) (hyp 0))`.

artifact paper_42 at sha256:bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb
policy strict-v1
use backends [nd@1]

claim c1
  nl      = "The safety invariant holds for deployment D"
  formal  = holds(safety_invariant, D)
  binding = { author = alice, rationale = "Certified citation of the audited safety invariant.", audit-status = reviewed }

leaf e1 : holds(safety_invariant, D)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = user
  refs       = [evidence/safety_audit.txt#section=invariants]

arg a1 : supports(c1) by certified_citation from [e1]
  assurance = cert(nd@1, sha256:strict-v1-theory-0, (app (lam h (atom 1:A5:holds1:L1:228:1:C16:safety_invariant1:L1:012:1:C1:D1:L1:0) (prem e1)) (prem e1)))

status c1

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: a1 (strict nd@1 redex) is unattacked -> in (grounded).
# Claim status:
#   c1 -> justified (a1 is a complete argument for it, with no attackers)
